WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.000
Movie Ancient Oriental Sciences

00:03.000 --> 00:11.000
In the foggy shadows of history, ancient eastern civilizations were brewing a scientific revolution that would change the world forever.

00:11.000 --> 00:18.000
These lands, rich in culture and intellect, were the cradle of scientific thought, a potent brew of insight and innovation.

00:18.000 --> 00:28.000
From the fertile plains of the Indus Valley, to the vibrant heart of Persia, to the towering peaks of China, a unique blend of curiosity and wisdom was taking shape.

00:28.000 --> 00:34.000
These civilizations, though separated by mountains and deserts, shared a common thread of scientific inquiry.

00:34.000 --> 00:43.000
They questioned, they pondered, they explored, they delved deep into the mysteries of the universe, uncovering truths that still hold relevance today.

00:43.000 --> 00:50.000
Their contributions were not just monumental, they were foundational, paving the way for future generations to build upon.

00:50.000 --> 00:54.000
Their wisdom was shrouded in mystery, yet their influence was undeniable.

00:55.000 --> 00:58.000
Their knowledge, though ancient, was far from primitive.

00:58.000 --> 01:03.000
The world was about to witness a scientific metamorphosis, sprung from the heart of the East.

01:03.000 --> 01:10.000
In the vast expanse of the unknown, the ancient Chinese gifted humanity its first guide, the compass.

01:10.000 --> 01:14.000
This invention, intriguingly, was not initially intended for navigation.

01:14.000 --> 01:22.000
Its earliest use was in geomancy and fortune-telling, serving as a spiritual guide that connected the terrestrial with the celestial.

01:22.000 --> 01:25.000
In time, the compass's purpose evolved.

01:25.000 --> 01:33.000
It was adapted into a practical tool that revolutionized seafaring, making it possible to traverse uncharted waters with confidence.

01:33.000 --> 01:40.000
This humble instrument, with its magnetized needle faithfully pointing north, ignited an era of exploration and discovery.

01:40.000 --> 01:45.000
Trade routes expanded, new lands were found, and the world as it was known began to change.

01:45.000 --> 01:51.000
The compass, in its silent, steadfast duty, was at the helm of this transformation.

01:51.000 --> 01:58.000
It directed explorers across vast oceans, through treacherous storms, and towards unimaginable discoveries.

01:58.000 --> 02:04.000
The compass was not merely a tool, it was the first step towards the interconnected world we know today.

02:04.000 --> 02:09.000
The whispers of the past, indeed, guide the symphony of the present.

02:09.000 --> 02:18.000
In a quest for immortality, the Chinese alchemists instead stumbled upon an invention that would forever alter the course of warfare, gunpowder.

02:18.000 --> 02:29.000
Imagine this. In the pursuit of eternal life, our ancestors, the Chinese alchemists, were mixing together a concoction of sulfur, charcoal and potassium nitrate.

02:29.000 --> 02:36.000
Little did they realize that their pursuit of immortality would lead them to create something that would profoundly change the world.

02:36.000 --> 02:42.000
Gunpowder. Ironically, the elixir of life they were seeking to concoct was nowhere in sight,

02:42.000 --> 02:47.000
but they had instead birthed a substance with a life-altering potential of a different kind.

02:47.000 --> 02:52.000
Initially, this black powder, as it was known, found its way into medicinal treatments.

02:52.000 --> 02:57.000
The alchemists believed it could treat skin diseases and kill parasites.

02:57.000 --> 03:00.000
It was even used as a fumigant to cleanse the air.

03:00.000 --> 03:04.000
However, it didn't take long for its explosive properties to be discovered.

03:04.000 --> 03:07.000
Once that happened, there was no turning back.

03:07.000 --> 03:11.000
The black powder was rapidly adapted for use in warfare.

03:11.000 --> 03:18.000
It started with simple firecrackers to scare off enemies, but soon it was being packed into bamboo tubes to create rudimentary bombs.

03:18.000 --> 03:23.000
And not long after, it was propelling arrows farther and faster than any archer could.

03:23.000 --> 03:27.000
And so the face of warfare was forever changed.

03:27.000 --> 03:35.000
The introduction of gunpowder weaponry shifted the dynamics on the battlefield, making it possible for smaller forces to defend against larger ones.

03:35.000 --> 03:41.000
The power of gunpowder spread beyond the east, reshaping global conflict and tilting the scales of power.

03:41.000 --> 03:47.000
From the castles of Europe to the samurai battles of Japan, gunpowder played a pivotal role.

03:47.000 --> 03:53.000
It brought about the end of the era of knights and catapults, ushering in the age of cannons and muskets.

03:53.000 --> 04:00.000
The landscape of power was forever altered, not by a quest for domination, but by a quest for life everlasting.

04:01.000 --> 04:07.000
Gunpowder, a testament to human ingenuity, forever changed the face of conflict and power dynamics.

04:07.000 --> 04:14.000
The ancient eastern sciences, shrouded in mystery, have left an indelible mark on the tapestry of human history.

04:14.000 --> 04:18.000
These sciences, as we've explored, were not merely isolated phenomena.

04:18.000 --> 04:28.000
They were the bedrock of transformative inventions like the compass and gunpowder, tools that forever changed our understanding of the world and our place within it.

04:28.000 --> 04:34.000
But the legacy of ancient eastern sciences extends far beyond these groundbreaking innovations.

04:34.000 --> 04:42.000
They laid the foundation for modern scientific thought, fostering an enduring curiosity about the natural world and the laws that govern it.

04:42.000 --> 04:51.000
The eastern sciences encouraged us to question, to explore and to seek answers, a philosophy that continues to guide our scientific inquiries today.

04:51.000 --> 05:00.000
From the way we navigate the oceans with the compass, to how we harness the power of chemicals in gunpowder, the influence of these ancient sciences is omnipresent.

05:00.000 --> 05:08.000
The echoes of these ancient eastern sciences still resonate in our world today, shaping the way we navigate and understand our lives.

